    <!-- Real Estate Coach Callout -->
    <div class="coach-callout">
      <h3>💡 Real Estate Coach's Take</h3>
      <p>
        Don't rely on a 10-minute Sunday open house visit to judge aircraft noise. Regional flight tracks shift between North Flow and South Flow depending on wind and weather patterns. I recommend a <strong>3-point field test</strong>: stand outside in the yard for 20 minutes during peak morning or evening departure windows, inspect the windows to see if acoustic double-pane or triple-pane retrofits are installed, and check if the home falls inside an official airport sound insulation grant boundary. In addition, installing high-efficiency MERV 13 or HEPA HVAC air filtration easily mitigates low-altitude jet fuel ultrafine particles (UFPs).
      </p>
    </div>

