      <h2>Boeing Field (KBFI): Cargo, Corporate & Boeing Testing Operations</h2>
      <p>
        While Sea-Tac handles the highest volume of commercial passenger traffic, <strong>Boeing Field (King County International Airport)</strong> is one of the busiest general aviation and cargo hubs in the nation. It operates 24 hours a day, 7 days a week.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Air Cargo & Freight Corridors:</strong> Major logistics carriers like UPS, DHL, and Amazon Air operate heavy jet freighters out of Boeing Field, frequently running late-night and early-morning departure schedules.</li>
        <li><strong>Boeing Military & Commercial Flight Testing:</strong> Boeing conducts initial flight testing, military aircraft transport (such as KC-46 tankers and P-8 Poseidons), and customer deliveries directly from the airfield.</li>
        <li><strong>Low-Altitude Flight Paths:</strong> Flight corridors run directly along the Duwamish River valley, passing over Georgetown, South Park, Beacon Hill, Tukwila, and parts of West Seattle.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Sea-Tac & Paine Field Operations</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Sea-Tac International Airport</strong> serves over 50 million commercial passengers annually. Departure and arrival corridors extend north over Beacon Hill and Seattle, and south over Des Moines and Federal Way. <strong>Paine Field</strong> in Snohomish County offers regional passenger flights alongside Boeing widebody jet assembly testing (777 and 767 models) and extensive flight training.
      </p>

      <h2>Air Quality & Sound Insulation Grants</h2>
      <p>
        Living under low-altitude flight paths involves two primary environmental factors: sound and air quality.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Airport Sound Insulation Programs:</strong> The Port of Seattle and regional airport authorities have funded extensive acoustic insulation programs for homes inside official 65 dB DNL noise contours. Upgrades include triple-pane acoustic windows, solid-core exterior doors, and attic insulation.</li>
        <li><strong>Ultrafine Particles (UFPs) & Air Filtration:</strong> Aircraft engines release microscopic ultrafine combustion particles during takeoff and landing. Using MERV 13 furnace filters or standalone HEPA air purifiers inside the home effectively traps airborne particulates.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

